BT 1 0 0 1 0 111 Tm 12 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (In 1972, Carl Sagan, Frank Drake, and Linda Salzman Sagan designed a 6x9 inch gold-anodized aluminum plaque and) Tj T* (bolted it to the antenna support struts of Pioneer 10. The plaque was intended as a message to any extraterrestrial) Tj T* (civilization that might intercept the spacecraft on its trajectory out of the solar system. In modern popular culture, Neil) Tj T* (deGrasse Tyson has claimed that the plaque's depiction of ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (nine planets) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( \(including Pluto\) is the one thing protecting Earth) Tj T* (from alien invasion -- because any civilization reading the plaque would search for solar systems with nine rocky/gaseous) Tj T* (bodies, and since four moons in our own system are larger than Pluto, the map would appear self-contradictory and) Tj T* (unreadable. This paper performs a complete word-for-word annotation of the plaque, then demonstrates rigorously why) Tj T* (Tyson's claim is ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (the smallest identifiable error on the map) Tj /F1 9 Tf (. The true interface failures lie elsewhere, and they are) Tj T* (catastrophic. The Mirror Interface Principle \(Papers 152, 153\) applied to the plaque reveals that Sagan solved the physics) Tj T* (and failed the interface -- the pulsar triangulation would locate Earth regardless of whether Pluto is counted as a planet.) Tj T* ET
